WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.795
- I'm Greg Jennings, and
this is Build Your Squad.

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:06.548
♪♪♪ Rhythmic music ♪♪♪

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.053
I'm here right now with B/R Gridiron

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:15.348
to build my all-time squad.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.182
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:20.395
OK, I am going to start

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.691
with my quarterback,

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.568
and this, for me, is rather easy,

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:27.652
and I'mma tell you why.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.238
I'm goin' with Tom Brady.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:34.617
He's the most clutch quarterback I've seen

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:39.414
in action, close-up, on television.

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:41.583
He has the most Super Bowls,

00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:44.711
so if I'm looking for
somebody to win me a game,

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.337
I'm goin' with that guy.

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:47.464
That's my guy.

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.715
I don't care what you say.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.716
That's my guy.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.092
[Clapping]

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:54.012
Next, running back.

00:00:54.012 --> 00:00:56.056
Now, you're gonna be
a little disappointed,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.557
possibly, maybe not.

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:58.850
I really don't care.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.936
We got the great Walter Payton.

00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:04.147
I love Walter Payton.

00:01:04.147 --> 00:01:06.274
I would put him there,

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:08.985
but then we got Jim Brown and we got all—

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.029
But I grew up in Michigan.

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:11.863
Hear me.

00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:13.281
I grew up in Michigan,

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:18.286
so I watched this guy my entire life.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:19.829
Special.

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.291
Said, "You know what?
I'm so special, I'm done.

00:01:23.291 --> 00:01:24.751
I don't even wanna play no more.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.711
I'm too good for this league."

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:28.922
That's not what he said, but
that's kinda what I felt like,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.926
because he was the only bright
spot on the Detroit Lions

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:36.221
and seemed to be the only
bright spot that ever existed

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:37.597
on the Detroit Lions.

00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:39.974
So, Barry Sanders.

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.351
Doesn't matter what you think.

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:42.477
That's my pick.

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.981
I'm going to skip this row
for now and come back later.

00:01:47.565 --> 00:01:49.359
I'm going to go to my defensive backs.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.863
And it's, it's rather easy.

00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.990
I mean, Prime.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.119
I mean, do I have to explain why?

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:03.498
I mean, the ultimate
prime-time playmaker.

00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:06.209
I mean, I got punt return covered.

00:02:06.209 --> 00:02:09.879
I got, I got all secondary levels covered

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:11.631
because he's done it all.

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.259
I can isolate him one-on-one.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:17.387
I can do whatever I need to do. We got it.

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:18.513
We good.

00:02:18.513 --> 00:02:20.181
And we the fastest man on the field,

00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:22.642
so I mean, need I say more?

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:27.814
I'm gonna go here to my
defensive end/linebacker.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.023
This is tough.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.233
This is really tough

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:33.695
because I played against this guy, Ray.

00:02:34.571 --> 00:02:37.740
I played against this guy, Derrick Brooks.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.909
I didn't play against Bruce Smith,

00:02:39.909 --> 00:02:41.953
although I recognize the greatness.

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:45.623
I did not play against
the great Reggie White,

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:49.169
although I respect and
realize how great he was.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.629
But Tecmo Bowl told me

00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:55.425
that Lawrence Taylor was that dude then,

00:02:55.425 --> 00:02:57.427
and I feel like if he played right now,

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:59.345
he would still be that dude.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.974
Just special. I mean, he was
the only player on Tecmo Bowl

00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:05.101
that could actually catch Bo Jackson.

00:03:05.101 --> 00:03:06.978
Like, and you can't catch Bo Jackson!

00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:07.896
Like, who—

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:09.022
what is that?

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.607
That's Lawrence Taylor, man.

00:03:10.607 --> 00:03:13.443
He created and pathed the way
for guys like Ray Lewis.

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:16.529
That's why I'm—that's why I gotta put
Lawrence Taylor there.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.031
And for receiver,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.490
now,

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:24.454
I know the pick, naturally,

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:27.540
everyone would say, "Oh,
I'm goin' Jerry Rice."

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.502
My favorite player, probably all-time.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.588
However...

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:36.716
"Who can make a play?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.761
I can!" And he can.

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:41.512
I'm not pickin' him right now,

00:03:41.512 --> 00:03:46.517
but that man right there,
he just was special.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.270
Randy Moss, man. I mean, it's like—

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.396
and I know you're gonna say,

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.731
"Aw, man, he was only a deep threat,

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:52.941
and he couldn't go across the middle."

00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:55.068
I don't care. I don't need
him to go across the middle.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:55.985
Do what you do.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:57.487
That's why he up here.

00:03:57.487 --> 00:03:59.530
That's why his face is here, and—

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.824
I mean, mine should've been,

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:03.701
but I told 'em, "Don't put it up there,"

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.411
cuz I don't wanna—

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.497
that's biased. I didn't wanna be that.

00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:09.415
And now I'mma lock my picks.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:12.877
This is my squad.

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:15.588
I don't care what you think.

00:04:16.464 --> 00:04:19.342
If you say, "Greg, naw, man,
whatchu—are you kidding me?"

00:04:19.342 --> 00:04:22.178
I'mma say, "So, yeah. I
guess I am kidding you."

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:23.471
If you say, "Greg, that's amazing.

00:04:23.471 --> 00:04:25.014
Now, I woulda had the same five,"

00:04:25.014 --> 00:04:26.975
I would say, "I know. That's
why I put 'em up there."

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.601
But these are my five.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.646
This who I'm goin' into any game with,

00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:33.439
and I'm winnin'.

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:36.192
And we gonna get a buncha these.

00:04:36.192 --> 00:04:37.318
A bunch of 'em.

